invariant: INV-38
file: tcp_nonblocking_frame.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh record_whole_len
reason: ch_record_whole_len calls a record whole one byte before its body
  has arrived, so its answer is one byte more than the caller holds, and
  a caller that passes that many bytes to ch_read reads one byte past its
  data. The record_whole_len harness requires every answer to lie within
  n, and to be the one tcp_nonblocking.h states.

--- old
    return rb_left(&r) < body_len ? 0 : REC_HDR + body_len;
--- new
    return rb_left(&r) + 1 < body_len ? 0 : REC_HDR + body_len;
